From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 06:42:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3ha9: Compute the gamma from the panel MTP

The gamma register values for every brightness level are not constants:
the panel is calibrated in the factory and carries the deviation of its
own gamma taps in MTP memory, from which the values have to be computed.
Without that the panel keeps the gamma it powers up with, so the
luminance of a step does not match what the AOR, ELVSS and VINT tables
aim for.

Port the vendor maths (LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820,
commit 7d08ec364a06, drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/panel/dimming.c):
rebuild the tap voltages from the MTP offsets, interpolate a 256 entry
gray scale between them, and for every level look the target voltages up
on the gamma curve and turn them back into register values. The per
panel tables are generated from the vendor headers.

Read the 34 MTP bytes with DCS 0xc8 once the DDIC is awake. The vendor
uses the same register, offset and length (S6E3HA9_MTP_REG,
S6E3HA9_MTP_OFS and S6E3HA9_MTP_LEN, s6e3ha9.h:39-41), and the data is
one time programmed, so one read per power on is enough. The resulting
per level gamma goes out with the rest of the brightness condition,
before the existing 0xf7 latch.

A panel that does not answer the read is not treated as fatal:
brightness stays monotonic through AOR, ELVSS and VINT and only the
photometric calibration of each step is lost, so the driver warns and
carries on.

The engine is a second object, so the driver becomes a composite module.
Its name does not change: the existing source file is renamed and
panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.o is built from both objects.

The arithmetic was checked against the vendor engine outside the tree,
by compiling both as user space programs and feeding them the same MTP
data: 74 of 74 levels come out byte identical for 7 different MTP sets.
Running it on the MTP of a real panel needs hardware and has not been
done yet.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
